  "Body": {
    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>Azure Functions support for&nbsp;PowerShell&nbsp;7.6&nbsp;is now&nbsp;available in preview.&nbsp;You can now develop apps using&nbsp;PowerShell&nbsp;7.6&nbsp;locally and deploy them to Azure Functions plans.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Learn more:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/scripting/whats-new/what-s-new-in-powershell-76?view=powershell-7.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">What's\nnew in&nbsp;PowerShell&nbsp;7.6</a>&nbsp;</li><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/supported-languages?tabs=isolated-process%2Cv4&amp;pivots=programming-language-powershell#languages-by-runtime-version\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Azure Functions&nbsp;PowerShell&nbsp;versions and their end\nof support dates</a>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/supported-languages?tabs=isolated-process%2Cv4&amp;pivots=programming-language-powershell#languages-by-runtime-version\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a></p>",
    "Markdown": "Azure Functions support for PowerShell 7.6 is now available in preview. You can now develop apps using PowerShell 7.6 locally and deploy them to Azure Functions plans.\n\nLearn more:\n\nWhat's\n\nnew in PowerShell 7.6\n\nAzure Functions PowerShell versions and their end\n\nof support dates"
  },
